ESP32 MPU6050 Step Counter with GC9A01 Round Display
Project Overview
This project uses an ESP32, MPU6050 accelerometer/gyroscope sensor, and a GC9A01 round TFT display to create a real-time step counter. The system detects walking movements using MPU6050 sensor data and displays the live step count on the round display.

Features
Real-time step counting
Live step display on GC9A01 round TFT screen
ESP32-based processing
MPU6050 motion sensing
Fitness tracker style interface
Serial Monitor debugging output

Hardware Required
ESP32 Development Board
MPU6050 Accelerometer & Gyroscope Sensor
GC9A01 Round TFT Display (240x240)
Jumper Wires
USB Cable

