How It Works
ESP32 reads acceleration data from the MPU6050 sensor.
Motion magnitude is calculated from X, Y, and Z acceleration values.
When the movement exceeds the step threshold, a step is detected.
The step counter increases automatically.
The GC9A01 display updates and shows the latest step count.
Step data is also printed to the Serial Monitor.

Upload Instructions
Install all required libraries.
Connect the MPU6050 and GC9A01 display according to the wiring tables.
Select "ESP32 Dev Module" in Arduino IDE.
Select the correct COM Port.
Upload the code to ESP32.
Open Serial Monitor at 115200 baud.
Start walking and observe the live step count on the display.

